The copy constructor is already minimal. Almost all of its cost is the `FieldBase` copy, which I can't touch here. The remaining members are a pointer, an index, a type tag and a bool, and the initializer list already copies each one directly with no extra work.

There is no safe change that would make this faster in any measurable way. So the version below behaves exactly the same and only changes the form: it copies each member with direct initialization from the source object. Expect no measurable speedup from this function alone.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile{field.profile},
      profileIndex{field.profileIndex},
      type{field.type},
      isFieldExpanded{field.isFieldExpanded}
{
}
```